# State Management

## Default: Cubit (not BLoC)

Use Cubit for 90% of cases. Only use full BLoC when you need `EventTransformer` (debounce, throttle, sequential).

```dart
@injectable
class LoginCubit extends Cubit<LoginState> {
  final AuthRepository _authRepository;
  LoginCubit(this._authRepository) : super(const LoginState.initial());
}
```

## States with Freezed

```dart
@freezed
abstract class LoginState with _$LoginState {
  const factory LoginState.initial() = _Initial;
  const factory LoginState.loading() = _Loading;
  const factory LoginState.success(UserModel user) = _Success;
  const factory LoginState.error(String message) = _Error;
}
```

## Rules

- Register cubits as `@injectable` (factory) so each route gets a fresh instance.
- Provide via GetIt: `create: (_) => getIt<MyCubit>()`.
- Catch `AppException` in cubits and emit error state with `e.message`.
- Keep UI dumb: pages only call cubit methods and react to state via `BlocConsumer`.
- Do NOT use Cubit + Freezed for trivial UI state (checkbox, dropdown). Use `StatefulWidget` or `ValueNotifier` instead.
